r introduction basis and scope). No unsupported mathematical implication is identified; this is a closure/format defect, not a claim that the theorem is false.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The proof's stated sources are the listed H003 and M001, M016, M013, M014, M018. The applications identify the spaces, sets and functions being substituted, and no additional ancestor or ambient premise is needed.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs\",\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/applications\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The local bounding argument and coordinate box estimate are valid. Product-box finiteness follows from the stated product-volume and interval-volume inputs plus the described countable finite-measure cover. From H003, smoothness, and the compact support obtained, the continuity/support assertions and the M001 integrability application follow. The calculation policy is not treated as importing a theorem.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\",\"/inference/applications\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Each listed input has an identifiable role: H003 supplies spatial constancy outside C; M016 bounds K; M013 and M014 establish finite box measure; M018 supplies closedness/Borel measurability; M001 supplies integrability. No hidden named analysis theorem is relied on.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\",\"/inference/applications\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The prose establishes the stated integrability, interval and compact-set witnesses, continuity and vanishing properties, and finite measure on compact sets for arbitrary t. The arbitrary t is discharged by the final generalization.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/1\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"t and K are treated arbitrarily and the witnesses J and C depend on t;